===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
[[File:Світанок на Сулі. Околиці села Малоселицького.jpg|thumb|dawn ({{senseno|en|Q193294}})]]

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[morning]] [[twilight]] period immediately before [[sunrise]].
# {{senseid|en|Q193294}} {{lb|en|countable}} The [[rising]] of the [[sun]].
#: {{syn|en|break of dawn|break of day|daybreak|day-dawn|dayspring|sunrise<id:Q193294>|Thesaurus:dawn}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1961|author={{w|Harry E. Wedeck}}|title=Dictionary of Aphrodisiacs|publisher=The Citadel Press|location=New York|page=209|passage=Every act of a Roman, from birth to death, from '''dawn''' to night, was controlled and supervised by some presiding deity.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[time]] when the sun rises.
#: {{syn|en|break of dawn|break of day|crack of dawn|daybreak|day-dawn|dayspring|sunrise||Thesaurus:dawn}}
#: {{ux|en|She rose before '''dawn''' to meet the train.}}
#: {{ux|en|The platoon braced itself for the '''dawn''' offensive.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[early|earliest]] [[phase]] of something.
#: {{syn|en|beginning|onset|start}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''dawn''' of civilization didn't imply twilight of barbarity.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1958 July|author=J. P. Wilson|title=Scottish Soliloquy|journal=Railway Magazine|page=495|text=In the Edinburgh area, Leith and neighbouring Granton have only one terminal station where formerly there were four, and the long-established ferry from Granton to Burntisland, the history of which stretches back to the '''dawn''' of Scottish railways, is no more.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-08-03|volume=408|issue=8847|magazine=w:The Economist| title=[http://www.economist.com/news/leaders/21582516-worlds-thirst-oil-could-be-nearing-peak-bad-news-producers-excellent Yesterday’s fuel]| passage=The '''dawn''' of the oil age was fairly recent. Although the stuff was used to waterproof boats in the Middle East 6,000 years ago, extracting it in earnest began only in 1859 after an oil strike in Pennsylvania. The first barrels of crude fetched $18 (around $450 at today’s prices).}}

