===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# That to which any person or thing is [[destined]]; a [[predetermined]] or [[inevitable]] eventual state; a condition [[predestine]]d by the Divine or by human will.
#: {{syn|en|fate|lot|orlay|Thesaurus:fate}}
#: {{ux|en|Death is the '''destiny''' of all mortal men.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1914|author=Li Ung Bing|chapter=The Second Joint Regency of the Empress|editor=Joseph Whiteside|title=Outlines of Chinese History|url=https://archive.org/details/outlinesofchines00liun/|location=Shanghai|publisher=w:The Commercial Press|OCLC=1687715|page=565|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/outlinesofchines00liun/page/565/|text=Her death (April 18, 1881) left the {{w|Empress Dowager Cixi|Empress Ts‘ŭ Hsi}}, the playmate of her youth, the sole Regent of China, with the '''destiny''' of four hundred millions of human beings in her hands.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1963|title=w:I Will Follow Him|lyricist=w:Norman Gimbel|composer=w:Franck Pourcel|artist=w:Peggy March|passage=And nothing can keep him from me / He is my '''destiny'''}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1977|album=Down to Love Town|author={{w|The Originals (group)|The Originals}}|title=Been Decided|text=Ain't no use to fight it / Don't tamper with my '''destiny''' / Any way you slice it / I'm in the hands of fate, you see}}
# One's eventual [[fate]] (not necessarily [[inevitable]] or [[predestine]]d).
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:"Weird Al" Yankovic|title=w:Christmas at Ground Zero|album=w:Polka Party!|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t039p6xqutU|year=1986|text=Everywhere the atom bombs are dropping / It's the end of all humanity / No more time for last-minute shopping / It's time to face your final '''destiny'''}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Bernard Louis De Koven|title=Hammocky Dreams|magazine=A Playful Path|url=https://www.aplayfulpath.com/hammocky-dreams/|date=2016-06-27|passage=Suspended between two ancient trees in some woody wonderland, the nearby brook babblingly bubbling to itself, the gently cooling breezes sweeping away all things bothersome, we self-sway each other to our own rhythms, and all our manifest '''destinies''' are ahhhsome.}}
# The fixed [[order]] of things; invincible [[necessity]]; an irresistible [[power]] or [[agency]] conceived of as determining the future, whether in general or of an individual.
#: {{syn|en|fate}}
#: {{ux|en|Dara doesn't believe in using dating apps - she insists that '''destiny''' will find her other half.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|author=Philip Pullman|title=Northern Lights|passage=There were two kinds of beardom opposed here, two futures, two '''destinies'''.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2007
|author=w:Drew Karpyshyn
|title={{w|Mass Effect: Revelation}}
|url=https://archive.org/details/masseffect00drew/
|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]
|publisher=w:Del Rey Books
|ISBN=978-0-345-49816-8
|OCLC=150381260
|pages=320–321
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/masseffect00drew/page/321/
|text=But it was much more than a mere ship. Its systems, processes, and technology were so advanced that they dwarfed every accomplishment of the Citadel species. Its grandeur and complexity rivaled the greatest creations of the Protheans—the mass relays and the Citadel. It may have even surpassed them. And if Saren could learn and understand how it worked, he could seize all that power for himself.<br>He’d spent his entire life preparing for a moment like this. Everything he’d ever done—his military service, his career with the Spectres—was only a prelude to this revelation. Now he had found his true purpose; '''destiny''' had led him here.}}

