====Usage notes====
* {{m|nb|den|Den}} agrees with both masculine and feminine singular nouns; {{m|nb|det}} is neuter singular and {{m|nb|de}} is plural.
* The following noun normally takes its definite form: ''den bilen'' ("that car"), ''den boka'' ("that book"). An adjective, when present, normally takes its definite form: ''den røde bilen'' ("that red car"). A noun without the definite suffix also occurs in literary or formal constructions, fixed expressions and phrases specified by a following clause or infinitive, such as ''den hensikt å ...'' ("the intention of ...").
* {{m|nb|denne}} ordinarily points to something nearer the speaker. {{m|nb|den}} may likewise refer to something nearby when combined with {{m|nb|her}}: ''den her boka'' or ''den boka her'' ("this book").
* Colloquial combinations also include ''den herre'' and ''den derre'', as in ''den derre bilen'' ("that car").

