====Usage notes====
* {{m|nb|den|Den}} has the same form as subject and object: ''den ligger her'' ("it is lying here"), ''jeg ser den'' ("I see it"). Its genitive is {{m|nb|dens}} ("its"); the corresponding neuter is {{m|nb|det}} (genitive {{m|nb|dets}}), and the plural personal pronoun is {{m|nb|de}} (object {{m|nb|dem}}, genitive {{m|nb|deres}}).
* Personal {{m|nb|den}} normally refers to things and animals; {{m|nb|han}} and {{m|nb|hun}} normally refer to people. Independent demonstrative {{m|nb|den}} can refer to a person, sometimes dismissively, and ''den som ...'' ("the one who ...; whoever ...") is ordinary usage. This differs from using personal {{m|nb|den}} as a general gender-neutral substitute for {{m|nb|han}} or {{m|nb|hun}}.
* The reflexive pronoun is {{m|nb|seg}}: ''Katten vasker seg'' ("The cat is washing itself").

