====Usage notes====
* The article is normally unstressed. Compare ''den røde bilen'' ("the red car") with stressed demonstrative ''den røde bilen'' ("that red car").
* Ordinary noun phrases normally have both the article and the noun's definite suffix: ''den gamle stolen'' ("the old chair"). Names, fixed expressions and some formal or literary phrases may lack the suffix: ''Den norske kirke'' ("the Church of Norway").

