# The act of [[determine|determining]], or the state of being [[determined]].
## {{lb|en|countable}} The act, process, or result of any accurate [[measurement]], as of length, volume, weight, intensity, etc.
##: {{ux|en|the '''determination''' of the wavelength of light}}
##: {{ux|en|the '''determination''' of the level of salt in sea water}}
##: {{ux|en|the '''determination''' of the oxygen in the air}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1951|month=March|author=J. H. Lehmann; A. D. Johnson; W. C. Bridges; J. Michel; D. M. Green|title=Cardiac Catheterization—A Diagnostic Aid in Congenital Heart Disease|journal=Northwest Medicine|volume=50|issue=3|location=Portland, Ore.|publisher=Northwest Medical Publishing Association|page=170|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/northwestmedicin5019nort/page/170/mode/2up?q=determinations|passage=Intracardiac blood pressures can be recorded by a simple water manometer or by electronic devices. These '''determinations''' are of value in identifying the different cardiac cavities.}}
## The act of defining a concept or notion by giving its essential constituents.
## The addition of a distinguishing feature to a concept or notion, thus limiting its extent.
##: {{antonyms|en|generalization}}
## The act of determining the relations of an object, such as genus and species; the referring of minerals, plants, or animals, to the species to which they belong; [[classification]]
##: {{ux|en|I am indebted to a friend for the '''determination''' of most of these shells.}}
# Direction or tendency to a certain end; impulsion.
#: {{syn|en|purpose}}
# The quality of mind which reaches definite conclusions; decisive character; resoluteness; [[fortitude]].
#: {{ux|en|Through sheer '''determination''', we managed to escape from the tornado.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The state of decision; a judicial decision, or ending of controversy.
# {{senseid|en|that which is determined upon}} {{lb|en|countable}} That which is determined upon; result of deliberation; purpose; conclusion formed; fixed [[resolution]].
#: {{syn|en|decision|conclusion|verdict|Thesaurus:judgement}}
#: {{ux|en|The tribunal has reached a '''determination''' in respect of this matter.}}
# A flow, rush, or tendency to a particular part
#: {{ux|en|a '''determination''' of blood to the head}}
# {{lb|en|law|otherwise|obsolete}} Bringing to an [[end]]; [[termination]]; limit.
#* {{quote-web|en|year=2021|author=HM Land Registry|work=Practice guide 26: leases – determination|url=https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/leases-determination/practice-guide-26-leases-determination|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20211004063807/https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/leases-determination/practice-guide-26-leases-determination|archivedate=4 October 2021|text=If a lease is determined by notice, forfeiture or frustration, all incumbrances will normally end automatically with the '''determination''' of the lease and can therefore be ignored.}}
