#: {{hypo|en|persistent depressive disorder<id:Q427810>|PDD<id:Q427810>|dysthymia<id:Q427810>|;|major depressive disorder<id:Q42844>|MDD<id:Q42844>|<|clinical depression#Noun}}
#: {{ux|en|I used to suffer from '''depression''', but now I'm mostly content with my life.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=William Styron|title=Why Primo Levi Need Not Have Died|work=The New York Times|date=1988-12-19|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1988/12/19/opinion/why-primo-levi-need-not-have-died.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=It is that Mr. Levi's death could not be dissociated from the major '''depression''' with which he was afflicted, and that indeed his suicide proceeded directly from that illness.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230402051745/https://www.nytimes.com/1988/12/19/opinion/why-primo-levi-need-not-have-died.html|archivedate=2 April 2023}}
# {{lb|en|psychology|countable}} A period of low [[morale]] or [[unhappiness]] (a period of experiencing the above-mentioned state of mind) which lasts longer than several weeks and may include [[ideation]] of self-inflicted injury or [[suicide]].
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2011-02-28|author=David J. Miklowitz|title=The Bipolar Disorder Survival Guide, Second Edition: What You and Your Family Need to Know|publisher=Guilford Press|isbn=9781609180140|page=106
|text={{...}} your illness reflects the textbook description of bipolar disorder (euphoric, grandiose, manic highs followed by deep '''depressions''',{{nb...}}}}
