# One appointed as the [[substitute]] of others, and [[empower]]ed to act for them, in their name or [[on behalf of|their behalf]]; a substitute in office.
#: {{syn|en|lieutenant|representative|delegate|vice|vicegerent|[[number two]] (infomal)}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''deputy''' of a prince}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''deputy''' sheriff was promoted after his senior retired.}}
#: {{ux|en|As the '''deputy''' store manager, he is able to fire staff.}}
# {{lb|en|mining|historical}} A person employed to install and remove [[prop]]s, [[brattice]]s, etc. and to clear [[gas]], for the safety of the [[miner]]s.
# {{lb|en|government}} The name for a member of [[legislature]] in some countries.
#: {{ux|en|The State [[Duma]] [[comprise]]s 450 '''deputies'''.}}
## A member of the French [[National Assembly]].
## {{lb|en|historical}} A member of the French [[Chamber of Deputies]], formerly called [[Corps Législatif]].
## {{lb|en|Ireland|often|capitalized}} A member of [[Dáil Éireann]], or the title of a member of Dáil Éireann.
##: {{ux|en|Eamon Ryan is a '''deputy''' in the Dáil.}}
##: {{ux|en|At today's meeting, '''Deputy''' Ryan will speak on local issues.}}
# {{lb|en|US|law enforcement}} a law enforcement officer who works for the county [[sheriff]]'s office; a deputy sheriff or sheriff's deputy; the entry level [[rank]] in such an agency.
#: {{ux|en|The sheriff's '''deputies''' took the suspect into custody.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Deputy''' Jones was promoted to [[corporal]] today.}}

====Usage notes====
''Deputy'' is used in combination with the names of various executive officers, to denote an assistant empowered to act in their name; as, ''deputy collector, deputy marshal, deputy sheriff.'' In the British coal mining industry, the word referred to as a deputy [[overman]], which was roughly akin to a foreman in other industries.

