===Etymology===
{{word|en|ine|dé}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*skend-}}
The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|descenden|t=to move downwards, fall, descend; to slope downwards; to go from a better to a worse condition, decline, degenerate; to be a descendant, derive from (a source); etc.}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=dē̆scenden|pos=v|id=MED11268}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|descendere}}, {{m|xno|descendre}}, and {{der|en|fro|descendere}}, {{m|fro|descendre|t=to move downwards, fall, descend; to slope downwards; to be a descendant, derive from (a source); etc.}} (modern {{cog|fr|descendre}}), and from their {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|dēscendere}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=7315183837|date=March 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref> the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{m|la|dēscendō|t=to come or go down, fall, descend; to slope downwards; to be a descendant; etc.}}, from {{m|la|de-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘from; down from’}} + {{m|la|scandō|t=to ascend, climb; to clamber}} (from {{der|en|ine-pro|*skend-|t=to climb, scale; to dart; to jump}}).

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from the verb.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=4491771519|date=July 2023}}</ref>

