##* {{RQ:Blackstone Commentaries|book=I|chapter=Of Corporations|page=469|passage=As to eleemoſynary corporations, by the [[dotation#Noun|dotation]] the founder and his heirs are of common right the legal viſitors, to ſee that that property is rightly employed, vvhich vvould otherwiſe have '''deſcended''' to the viſitor himſelf: {{...}}}}
